00:31:54.166 --> 00:31:56.930
This is slightly easier to
install and maintain because

00:31:56.931 --> 00:31:58.180
here the problem is if

00:31:58.181 --> 00:31:59.565
you have your large switch
in the middle,

00:31:59.566 --> 00:32:00.890
you need to route all cables

00:32:00.891 --> 00:32:02.290
somehow through real space into

00:32:02.291 --> 00:32:03.880
that middle thing and

00:32:03.881 --> 00:32:05.160
they're usually
becomes a total mess.

00:32:05.161 --> 00:32:06.500
Well if you do this,

00:32:06.501 --> 00:32:08.110
you have a nice distribution of

00:32:08.111 --> 00:32:09.705
your cables throughout
the whole data center,

00:32:09.706 --> 00:32:12.010
you don't have the one point
of failure also,

00:32:12.011 --> 00:32:13.420
so usually people like

00:32:13.421 --> 00:32:15.780
this in practice this
looks better in theory.

00:32:15.781 --> 00:32:18.620
Okay and now, of course
