00:35:55.296 --> 00:35:57.805
Let them fail. So,
we will get to this.

00:35:57.806 --> 00:35:59.885
I'm a big fan of
failing place networking

00:35:59.886 --> 00:36:02.035
because you cannot
pull the cable anyway,

00:36:02.036 --> 00:36:04.360
like if you have cable

00:36:04.361 --> 00:36:09.190
like fiber cable lying in
the cable lying enclosure,

00:36:09.191 --> 00:36:10.590
and our cable lying
enclosure even for

00:36:10.591 --> 00:36:12.585
the blue water system
was like this thick,

00:36:12.586 --> 00:36:15.090
and for the park system

00:36:15.091 --> 00:36:17.460
that they were planning that
would have been like this.

00:36:17.461 --> 00:36:21.300
There was a completely crazy
system and I don't know

00:36:21.301 --> 00:36:22.930
100 kilometers of cable or so

00:36:22.931 --> 00:36:25.615
was the deal for that system,

00:36:25.616 --> 00:36:28.210
but you don't worry about
it, you put them in,

00:36:28.211 --> 00:36:30.430
and the idea for
these systems was actually

00:36:30.431 --> 00:36:33.050
just throw a new cable
over the old ones.

00:36:33.051 --> 00:36:36.920
But, most topologies
actually degrade gracefully.

00:36:36.921 --> 00:36:39.180
The torus does not,

00:36:39.181 --> 00:36:40.600
but dragonfly does and

00:36:40.601 --> 00:36:42.255
slim fly does as we'll
see in a minute.

00:36:42.256 --> 00:36:43.620
So, which means if a cable fails

00:36:43.621 --> 00:36:45.270
other routing will
fix it, no worries.

00:36:45.271 --> 00:36:48.255
As long as not more than 10
percent of your cables fail,

00:36:48.256 --> 00:36:50.520
you will not lose
more than 10 percent of

00:36:50.521 --> 00:36:51.735
your bandwidth and in fact it

00:36:51.736 --> 00:36:53.180
even degrades
gracefully afterwards.

00:36:53.181 --> 00:36:54.500
So, if you lose 20 percent
of your cables,

00:36:54.501 --> 00:36:55.740
you lose 20 percent eventually.

