But it behaves similarly,

00:40:29.951 --> 00:40:31.080
I would strongly suspect.

00:40:31.081 --> 00:40:32.830
So, we didn't look
at node failures,

00:40:32.831 --> 00:40:35.320
only at cable failures,
or link failures.

00:40:35.321 --> 00:40:37.400
Okay. So, then we could
talk about routing

00:40:37.401 --> 00:40:39.450
but let me skip this in
the interest of time because,

00:40:39.451 --> 00:40:40.620
again, you can use

00:40:40.621 --> 00:40:41.760
