00:41:14.031 --> 00:41:16.135
So, it's not our simulator,
that's what I want to say.

00:41:16.136 --> 00:41:18.840
It's a real setting.
How does this work?

00:41:18.841 --> 00:41:21.200
So, again, slightly if you're not

00:41:21.201 --> 00:41:23.020
used to looking at
these networking plots,

00:41:23.021 --> 00:41:23.995
let me explain this.

00:41:23.996 --> 00:41:26.315
So we have a latency,
this is basically,

00:41:26.316 --> 00:41:28.790
we have an all to all pattern,
as I mentioned earlier.

00:41:28.791 --> 00:41:30.990
Every node injects packets

00:41:30.991 --> 00:41:33.290
