00:41:52.656 --> 00:41:56.270
So, zero offered load
until one offered load.

00:41:56.271 --> 00:41:58.920
Ideally, and
then the latency here.

00:41:58.921 --> 00:42:02.090
So what happens, if you
push data into a network,

00:42:02.091 --> 00:42:03.820
all of those plots are
very characteristic.

00:42:03.821 --> 00:42:05.285
They start at the latency.

00:42:05.286 --> 00:42:06.390
This is the lowest,

00:42:06.391 --> 00:42:08.625
it's basically your diameter
of the network.

00:42:08.626 --> 00:42:10.320
You can see Slim Fly
always best in terms of

00:42:10.321 --> 00:42:12.960
latency because the
diameter is lowest.

00:42:12.961 --> 00:42:15.310
So, this thing here,

00:42:15.311 --> 00:42:17.215
Slim Fly with minimum routing,

00:42:17.216 --> 00:42:19.525
this is Slim Fly with
another routing,

00:42:19.526 --> 00:42:22.065
this is Fat Tree up here,

00:42:22.066 --> 00:42:23.795
and then it's Dragonfly here.

00:42:23.796 --> 00:42:25.520
You see Slim Fly diameter two,

00:42:25.521 --> 00:42:28.110
Dragonfly diameter three,
Fat Tree diameter four.

00:42:28.111 --> 00:42:30.065
So, you can see this
